<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30063" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">murra</span></b>  (less correctly <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">murrha</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">myrrha</span></b> ), ae, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μύρρα</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A stone of which costly vessels</i> (v. murrinus
			and murreus) <i>were made</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">maculosae pocula murrae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. 10, 80, 1</span></i>
			; hence, <b>poet.</b> transf., <i>vessels of murra, murrine vases</i>, <i><span class="en">id. 4,
			86</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The myrrh-tree</i> and <i>myrrh</i>,
			v. myrrha. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Murra</span></b> , <i>the name
				of a horse</i>, perh. of a spotted one, <i><span class="en">Inscr.
					Grut. 341</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
